{"name":"Starch","hex":"#ac9a6c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"starch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A widely diffused vegetable substance, found in seeds, bulbs and tubers, as extracted (e.g. from potatoes, corn, rice, etc.) in the form of a white, glistening, granular or powdery substance, without taste or smell, and giving a very peculiar creaking sound when rubbed between the fingers. It is used as a food, in the production of commercial grape sugar, for stiffening linen in laundries, in making paste, etc.","Carbohydrates, as with grain and potato based foods."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply or treat with laundry starch, in order to create a hard, smooth surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Starch","blocks":[{"text":"Starch is a carbohydrate consisting of numerous glucose units joined by glycosidic bonds. This polysaccharide is produced by most green plants for energy storage. Worldwide, it is the most common carbohydrate in human diets, and is contained in large amounts in staple foods such as wheat, potatoes, maize (corn), rice, and cassava (manioc)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornstarch_mixed_with_water.jpg/330px-Cornstarch_mixed_with_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starch"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png/500px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png/1280px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png/500px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Starch is composed of glucose monomers linked by α-1,4-glycosidic bonds sometimes with α-1,6 branches is used for energy storage in plants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AXBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Starch.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Starch_granules_of_potato02.jpg/500px-Starch_granules_of_potato02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Starch_granules_of_potato02.jpg/1280px-Starch_granules_of_potato02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Starch_granules_of_potato02.jpg/500px-Starch_granules_of_potato02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Potato starch granules in cells of the potato","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStarch_granules_of_potato02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Starch_Granules_in_Endosperm_of_Zea_Mays_Embryo_by_Phase_Contrast_%2840725881153%29.jpg/500px-Starch_Granules_in_Endosperm_of_Zea_Mays_Embryo_by_Phase_Contrast_%2840725881153%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Starch_Granules_in_Endosperm_of_Zea_Mays_Embryo_by_Phase_Contrast_%2840725881153%29.jpg/1280px-Starch_Granules_in_Endosperm_of_Zea_Mays_Embryo_by_Phase_Contrast_%2840725881153%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Starch_Granules_in_Endosperm_of_Zea_Mays_Embryo_by_Phase_Contrast_%2840725881153%29.jpg/500px-Starch_Granules_in_Endosperm_of_Zea_Mays_Embryo_by_Phase_Contrast_%2840725881153%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o